From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shupeng Xue <dspxue@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:11:55 +1100
Subject: [PATCH wireless-next 03/21] wifi: b43: return -EOPNOTSUPP for ciphers
 the hardware can't do

Since b43 advertises MFP, mac80211 hands it the BIP key of every
connection with management frame protection, and possibly GCMP keys.
b43_op_set_key() treats any cipher other than WEP, TKIP and CCMP as a
driver bug: it warns (with CONFIG_B43_DEBUG) and returns -EINVAL, and
mac80211 logs

  failed to set key (4, ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff) to hardware (-22)

on every connection before falling back to software crypto.

Return -EOPNOTSUPP, which tells mac80211 to do the cipher in software
without complaint (see "Hardware crypto acceleration" in mac80211.h
and ieee80211_key_enable_hw_accel()), as ath5k and ath9k do; ath5k had
the same warning, removed in commit a70e1d6fd6b5 ("ath5k: drop bogus
warning on drv_set_key with unsupported cipher").

Tested on a BCM4331 against an AP with optional PMF: the warning and
the error message are gone, BIP is done in software as before.

Fixes: 75d057bda1fb ("b43: Fix connection problem with WPA3")
Assisted-by: pi:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
index 817448e58e7f..13f6d9623c8a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -4222,7 +4222,8 @@ static int b43_op_set_key(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, enum set_key_cmd cmd,
 		algorithm = B43_SEC_ALGO_AES;
 		break;
 	default:
-		B43_WARN_ON(1);
+		/* e.g. BIP for MFP: mac80211 does it in software */
+		err = -EOPNOTSUPP;
 		goto out_unlock;
 	}
 	index = (u8) (key->keyidx);
